        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            An air purifier and a dehumidifier answer different questions. If the air has too much water in it, only a dehumidifier helps; if it has too many particles in it, only a purifier does. Measure humidity before you spend anything, because that one number decides most cases.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For mold, the order is fixed: stop the water, dry the space to 45 to 50 percent, clean the growth with a purifier running, then keep the dehumidifier on for the space and the purifier near the people. Doing it the other way round buys clean air for a room that is still making the problem.
          </p>
        </div>

